        <Desc>Worship program - CHRIST UNITED METHODIST MINISTRY CENTER PROVIDES WORSHIP SPACE AND MEETING FACILITIES EACH WEEK FOR TEN CONGREGATIONS. IN 2015, FOUR CONGREGATIONS INCLUDING AFRICAN AMERICAN, HISPANIC, HAITIAN CONGREGATIONS ALONG WITH THE LEGACY CONGREATION OF CHRIST UNITED METHODIST CHURCH (CALLED CHRIST CHAPEL) JOINED TO FORM EXODUS UNITED METHODIST CHURCH. THE OTHER CONGREGATIONS WORSHIPING AT THE FACILITIES REFLECT A DIVERSITY IN CHRISTIAN COMMUNITIES, INCLUDING ADVENTIST, MARSHALLESE UCC, ERITREAN CHRISTIAN, AME ZION, AND AN INDEPENDENT HISPANIC FELLOWSHIP. BEFORE THE PANDEMIC IN 2020, 400 PEOPLE WORSHIPED EACH WEEK IN ONE OF THE CHURCHES THAT USE CHRIST UNITED METHODIST MINISTRY CENTER'S SANCUARY, CHAPEL AND FACILITIES. TODAY THAT NUMBER IS 600 WORSHIPPERS PER WEEK REPRESENTING 10 CONGREGATIONS.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActyOtherGrp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActyOtherGrp>
        <ExpenseAmt>27414</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>Medical Clinic program - CMC OPERATES FREE CLINICS BY APPOINTMENT, PRIMARILY THROUGH TELEMEDICINE. CHRIST MINISTRY CENTER (CMC) ALSO HOSTS BLOOD DRIVES FOR THE SAN DIEGO BLOOD BANK, WITH AN AVERAGE OF 22 UNITS OF BLOOD COLLECTED AT EACH. EACH UNIT OF BLOOD COLLECTED HAS THE POTENTIAL TO SAVE THREE LIVES. CMC ALSO HOSTS LIFELINE SCREENING EVENTS WHEREIN PERSONS SIGNED UP TO HAVE MEDICAL TESTS AND EVALUATIONS PERFORMED BY LIFELINE SCREENINGS.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActyOtherGrp>
